{
  "title": "Stage 5: Policy rules",
  "summary": "Flag expenses that are valid but need a human: rules written as patterns, reasons written with a switch.",
  "minutes": 20,
  "prereqs": [
    "csharp/05-robust-code/03-pattern-matching",
    "csharp/02-control-flow/02-switch"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Valid is not the same as acceptable",
      "body": [
        "Every expense the program keeps is now well formed. That does not make it fine. A 600.00 hotel bill is a perfectly valid row, and somebody in finance still wants to look at it.",
        "",
        "Companies write these expectations down as **policy rules**. This stage teaches your tool four of them:",
        "",
        "| Rule | Flag when |",
        "|---|---|",
        "| Meal limit | a `Meals` expense is over 50.00 |",
        "| Large expense | any expense is over 500.00 |",
        "| Weekend travel | a `Travel` expense is dated Saturday or Sunday |",
        "| Missing description | the description is empty |",
        "",
        "A flagged expense is **not** rejected. It still counts in every total. It is also listed in a new section, with the reason:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Needs review: 4",
        "  2026-03-07 Travel 120.00: travel on a weekend",
        "  2026-03-09 Lodging 600.00: over 500.00",
        "  2026-03-11 Meals 65.20: meal over 50.00",
        "  2026-04-02 Meals 18.00: missing description",
        "```",
        "",
        "One expense can break several rules, and then it shows all of them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sort",
      "prompt": "Rejected or flagged? A rejected row cannot be read as an expense at all. A flagged one is a real expense that a person should look at.",
      "buckets": [
        "Rejected",
        "Flagged"
      ],
      "items": [
        [
          "`2026-03-06,Supplies,abc,Printer paper`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`2026-03-09,Lodging,600.00,Hotel`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`2026-03-05,Meals`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`2026-03-07,Travel,120.00,Train` (a Saturday)",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`2026-03-10,Parking,8.00,Car park`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`2026-04-02,Meals,18.00,` (no description)",
          1
        ]
      ],
      "explain": "`abc` is not an amount, two columns are not four, and `Parking` is not a category: those rows carry no usable expense. The other three are complete, countable expenses that happen to break a policy."
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Rules as patterns",
      "body": [
        "A rule is a question about the **shape** of an expense, which is what property patterns are for. The braces list the properties you care about and what each must look like:",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "if (expense is { Category: Category.Meals, Amount: > 50m })",
        "    flags.Add(Flag.MealOverLimit);",
        "```",
        "",
        "Read it as: *an expense whose category is Meals and whose amount is over 50*. Both parts must match.",
        "",
        "Collect the flags in a list, with one separate `if` per rule. Not `else if`: each rule gets its say, so one expense can pick up several flags.",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "List<Flag> CheckPolicy(Expense expense)",
        "{",
        "    var flags = new List<Flag>();",
        "",
        "    if (expense is { Category: Category.Meals, Amount: > MealLimit })",
        "        flags.Add(Flag.MealOverLimit);",
        "    if (expense.Amount > LargeExpenseLimit)",
        "        flags.Add(Flag.LargeExpense);",
        "",
        "    return flags;",
        "}",
        "",
        "enum Flag { MealOverLimit, LargeExpense }",
        "```",
        "",
        "The limits are named constants, declared once near the top of the file. A bare `50` in the middle of a method tells the reader nothing. `MealLimit` says what it is, and there is one place to change it.",
        "",
        "```csharp",
        "const decimal MealLimit = 50m;",
        "const decimal LargeExpenseLimit = 500m;",
        "```",
        "",
        "The flag is an enum, not a message. What a flag *means* and how it is *worded* are separate decisions, and a `switch` expression turns one into the other when it is time to print."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Each rule is its own `if`. What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "var expense = new Expense(\"Meals\", 80m);",
        "",
        "if (expense is { Category: \"Meals\", Amount: > 50m })",
        "    Console.WriteLine(\"meal over limit\");",
        "if (expense is { Amount: > 500m })",
        "    Console.WriteLine(\"large\");",
        "if (expense is { Category: \"Travel\" } or { Amount: > 75m })",
        "    Console.WriteLine(\"check\");",
        "",
        "record Expense(string Category, decimal Amount);"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "meal over limit",
        "check"
      ],
      "explain": "The first pattern matches: Meals, and 80 is over 50. The second does not: 80 is not over 500. The third joins two patterns with `or`, and the second half matches because 80 is over 75."
    },
    {
      "type": "blanks",
      "prompt": "Complete the rule that flags a meal costing more than 50.",
      "code": [
        "if (expense __1__ { Category: Category.Meals, Amount: __2__ 50m })",
        "    flags.__3__(Flag.MealOverLimit);"
      ],
      "blanks": [
        "is",
        ">",
        "Add"
      ],
      "bank": [
        "==",
        "<",
        "as",
        "Remove"
      ],
      "explain": "`is` tests a value against a pattern. Inside the pattern, `> 50m` is a relational pattern: there is no variable on its left, because the property name before the colon says what is being compared."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Flag expensive items",
      "carry": true,
      "prompt": [
        "Add policy checking with the first two rules.",
        "",
        "1. Near the top of the file, declare the constants `MealLimit` (50) and `LargeExpenseLimit` (500).",
        "2. Add `enum Flag { MealOverLimit, LargeExpense }` and the record `FlaggedExpense(Expense Expense, List<Flag> Flags)`.",
        "3. Write `List<Flag> CheckPolicy(Expense expense)`. A `Meals` expense **over** 50.00 gets `MealOverLimit`. Any expense **over** 500.00 gets `LargeExpense`. Exactly 50.00 or 500.00 is allowed.",
        "4. Write `string Explain(Flag flag)` with a `switch` expression: `meal over 50.00` and `over 500.00`. Build the text from the constants so the two can never disagree.",
        "5. Write `void PrintNeedsReview(List<Expense> expenses)` and call it after the month section.",
        "",
        "The section is an empty line, `Needs review: N`, then one line per flagged expense in input order: two spaces, the date, the category, the amount as `N2`, a colon, and the reasons joined by `, `.",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Expenses: 6",
        "Total: 860.70",
        "Average: 143.45",
        "Largest: 600.00 (Lodging, 2026-03-09)",
        "",
        "By category",
        "Lodging           600.00",
        "Travel            165.50",
        "Meals              95.20",
        "",
        "By month",
        "2026-03           842.70",
        "2026-04            18.00",
        "",
        "Needs review: 2",
        "  2026-03-09 Lodging 600.00: over 500.00",
        "  2026-03-11 Meals 65.20: meal over 50.00",
        "",
        "Rejected: 5",
        "  line 4: expected 4 columns but found 2",
        "  line 6: invalid amount 'abc'",
        "  line 9: invalid date '2026-13-01'",
        "  line 10: unknown category 'Parking'",
        "  line 11: amount must be positive",
        "```",
        "",
        "An expense with both flags lists them in the order above: `meal over 50.00, over 500.00`. With nothing flagged, print `Needs review: 0`."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "using System.Globalization;",
        "",
        "var expenses = new List<Expense>();",
        "var rejected = new List<Rejected>();",
        "",
        "var lineNumber = 0;",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    lineNumber++;",
        "    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line)) continue;",
        "    if (line.StartsWith(\"date,\")) continue;",
        "",
        "    var result = ParseLine(lineNumber, line);",
        "    if (result is Parsed parsed)",
        "        expenses.Add(parsed.Expense);",
        "    else if (result is Rejected rejection)",
        "        rejected.Add(rejection);",
        "}",
        "",
        "if (expenses.Count == 0)",
        "{",
        "    Console.WriteLine(\"No valid expenses.\");",
        "}",
        "else",
        "{",
        "    PrintSummary(expenses);",
        "    PrintByCategory(expenses);",
        "    PrintByMonth(expenses);",
        "}",
        "",
        "PrintRejected(rejected);",
        "",
        "ParseResult ParseLine(int lineNumber, string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',', 4, StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);",
        "",
        "    if (parts.Length != 4)",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"expected 4 columns but found {parts.Length}\");",
        "",
        "    if (!DateOnly.TryParseExact(parts[0], \"yyyy-MM-dd\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.None, out var date))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"invalid date '{parts[0]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (!Enum.TryParse<Category>(parts[1], ignoreCase: true, out var category) || !Enum.IsDefined(category))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"unknown category '{parts[1]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (!decimal.TryParse(parts[2], CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out var amount))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"invalid amount '{parts[2]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (amount <= 0)",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, \"amount must be positive\");",
        "",
        "    return new Parsed(new Expense(date, category, amount, parts[3]));",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintSummary(List<Expense> expenses)",
        "{",
        "    var largest = expenses.OrderByDescending(e => e.Amount).First();",
        "",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Expenses: {expenses.Count}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Total: {expenses.Sum(e => e.Amount):N2}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Average: {expenses.Average(e => e.Amount):N2}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Largest: {largest.Amount:N2} ({largest.Category}, {largest.Date:yyyy-MM-dd})\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintByCategory(List<Expense> expenses)",
        "{",
        "    var rows = expenses",
        "        .GroupBy(e => e.Category)",
        "        .Select(g => new SummaryRow(g.Key.ToString(), g.Sum(e => e.Amount)))",
        "        .OrderByDescending(row => row.Total);",
        "",
        "    PrintTable(\"By category\", rows);",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintByMonth(List<Expense> expenses)",
        "{",
        "    var rows = expenses",
        "        .GroupBy(e => e.Date.ToString(\"yyyy-MM\"))",
        "        .OrderBy(g => g.Key)",
        "        .Select(g => new SummaryRow(g.Key, g.Sum(e => e.Amount)));",
        "",
        "    PrintTable(\"By month\", rows);",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintTable(string heading, IEnumerable<SummaryRow> rows)",
        "{",
        "    Console.WriteLine();",
        "    Console.WriteLine(heading);",
        "    foreach (var row in rows)",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"{row.Name,-12}{row.Total,12:N2}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintRejected(List<Rejected> rejected)",
        "{",
        "    Console.WriteLine();",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Rejected: {rejected.Count}\");",
        "    foreach (var rejection in rejected)",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"  line {rejection.LineNumber}: {rejection.Reason}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "enum Category { Travel, Meals, Lodging, Supplies, Other }",
        "",
        "record Expense(DateOnly Date, Category Category, decimal Amount, string Description);",
        "",
        "abstract record ParseResult;",
        "",
        "record Parsed(Expense Expense) : ParseResult;",
        "",
        "record Rejected(int LineNumber, string Reason) : ParseResult;",
        "",
        "record SummaryRow(string Name, decimal Total);"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "using System.Globalization;",
        "",
        "const decimal MealLimit = 50m;",
        "const decimal LargeExpenseLimit = 500m;",
        "",
        "var expenses = new List<Expense>();",
        "var rejected = new List<Rejected>();",
        "",
        "var lineNumber = 0;",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    lineNumber++;",
        "    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line)) continue;",
        "    if (line.StartsWith(\"date,\")) continue;",
        "",
        "    var result = ParseLine(lineNumber, line);",
        "    if (result is Parsed parsed)",
        "        expenses.Add(parsed.Expense);",
        "    else if (result is Rejected rejection)",
        "        rejected.Add(rejection);",
        "}",
        "",
        "if (expenses.Count == 0)",
        "{",
        "    Console.WriteLine(\"No valid expenses.\");",
        "}",
        "else",
        "{",
        "    PrintSummary(expenses);",
        "    PrintByCategory(expenses);",
        "    PrintByMonth(expenses);",
        "    PrintNeedsReview(expenses);",
        "}",
        "",
        "PrintRejected(rejected);",
        "",
        "ParseResult ParseLine(int lineNumber, string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',', 4, StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);",
        "",
        "    if (parts.Length != 4)",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"expected 4 columns but found {parts.Length}\");",
        "",
        "    if (!DateOnly.TryParseExact(parts[0], \"yyyy-MM-dd\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.None, out var date))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"invalid date '{parts[0]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (!Enum.TryParse<Category>(parts[1], ignoreCase: true, out var category) || !Enum.IsDefined(category))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"unknown category '{parts[1]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (!decimal.TryParse(parts[2], CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out var amount))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"invalid amount '{parts[2]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (amount <= 0)",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, \"amount must be positive\");",
        "",
        "    return new Parsed(new Expense(date, category, amount, parts[3]));",
        "}",
        "",
        "List<Flag> CheckPolicy(Expense expense)",
        "{",
        "    var flags = new List<Flag>();",
        "",
        "    if (expense is { Category: Category.Meals, Amount: > MealLimit })",
        "        flags.Add(Flag.MealOverLimit);",
        "    if (expense.Amount > LargeExpenseLimit)",
        "        flags.Add(Flag.LargeExpense);",
        "",
        "    return flags;",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Explain(Flag flag) => flag switch",
        "{",
        "    Flag.MealOverLimit => $\"meal over {MealLimit:N2}\",",
        "    Flag.LargeExpense => $\"over {LargeExpenseLimit:N2}\",",
        "    _ => throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException(nameof(flag))",
        "};",
        "",
        "void PrintSummary(List<Expense> expenses)",
        "{",
        "    var largest = expenses.OrderByDescending(e => e.Amount).First();",
        "",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Expenses: {expenses.Count}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Total: {expenses.Sum(e => e.Amount):N2}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Average: {expenses.Average(e => e.Amount):N2}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Largest: {largest.Amount:N2} ({largest.Category}, {largest.Date:yyyy-MM-dd})\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintByCategory(List<Expense> expenses)",
        "{",
        "    var rows = expenses",
        "        .GroupBy(e => e.Category)",
        "        .Select(g => new SummaryRow(g.Key.ToString(), g.Sum(e => e.Amount)))",
        "        .OrderByDescending(row => row.Total);",
        "",
        "    PrintTable(\"By category\", rows);",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintByMonth(List<Expense> expenses)",
        "{",
        "    var rows = expenses",
        "        .GroupBy(e => e.Date.ToString(\"yyyy-MM\"))",
        "        .OrderBy(g => g.Key)",
        "        .Select(g => new SummaryRow(g.Key, g.Sum(e => e.Amount)));",
        "",
        "    PrintTable(\"By month\", rows);",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintTable(string heading, IEnumerable<SummaryRow> rows)",
        "{",
        "    Console.WriteLine();",
        "    Console.WriteLine(heading);",
        "    foreach (var row in rows)",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"{row.Name,-12}{row.Total,12:N2}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintNeedsReview(List<Expense> expenses)",
        "{",
        "    var flagged = expenses",
        "        .Select(e => new FlaggedExpense(e, CheckPolicy(e)))",
        "        .Where(f => f.Flags.Count > 0)",
        "        .ToList();",
        "",
        "    Console.WriteLine();",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Needs review: {flagged.Count}\");",
        "    foreach (var item in flagged)",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"  {DescribeFlagged(item)}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "string DescribeFlagged(FlaggedExpense flagged)",
        "{",
        "    var expense = flagged.Expense;",
        "    var reasons = string.Join(\", \", flagged.Flags.Select(Explain));",
        "",
        "    return $\"{expense.Date:yyyy-MM-dd} {expense.Category} {expense.Amount:N2}: {reasons}\";",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintRejected(List<Rejected> rejected)",
        "{",
        "    Console.WriteLine();",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Rejected: {rejected.Count}\");",
        "    foreach (var rejection in rejected)",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"  line {rejection.LineNumber}: {rejection.Reason}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "enum Category { Travel, Meals, Lodging, Supplies, Other }",
        "",
        "record Expense(DateOnly Date, Category Category, decimal Amount, string Description);",
        "",
        "abstract record ParseResult;",
        "",
        "record Parsed(Expense Expense) : ParseResult;",
        "",
        "record Rejected(int LineNumber, string Reason) : ParseResult;",
        "",
        "record SummaryRow(string Name, decimal Total);",
        "",
        "enum Flag { MealOverLimit, LargeExpense }",
        "",
        "record FlaggedExpense(Expense Expense, List<Flag> Flags);"
      ],
      "tests": [
